==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*hirvas}}, from {{etyl|ine-bsl-pro|fi}} {{m|ine-bsl-pro|*śirwas}}. Cognate with Northern Sami {{m|se|sarvvis}}, which must have either been borrowed directly from Balto-Slavic or (more likely) come via Finnic before *š became h.

